i'm not following you here. the other ideas deleted were mostly about
disseminating more information to all players. is that bad? the ideas
you especially targeted were related *only* to dlev1 not the earlier
levels in general, just dlev1 (i.e. no surprises, just the kill the
monsters that appear). perhaps you meant the ideas were bad because
they were evil and insidious or perhaps you were making a joke on the
fact that "bad" and "off the wall" are both michael jackson albums???

game "balance", in my opinion, demands that altars be removed from dlev1 as
well as the other things which can get you killed (i.e. it can't be too easy).
given the high-threshold against early survival in nh3 the original post
was written in the spirit of offing the wall. in any event, it's somewhat
of a moot point given the imminent distribution of patchlevel 6 which,
in part, addresses the early survival problem.

*Your* explore-mode suggestion regarding a separate scoreboard has merit.
however, it could also foster a "kiddyland" milieu. obviously, i favor
one scoreboard where everybody's name can be seen up there in lights.

